            <ArticleTitle>Flow reversal in coronary collaterals.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1346-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of collateral flow reversal observed seven months after angioplasty and due to the progression of a second lesion in another vessel. Such an occurrence has not been reported previously in association with angioplasty. Its clinical implications are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
